# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  prod profile — LOCAL config only.  Copy to  config/prod.properties  (gitignored).
#
#  On Render / any real host: DON'T use this file — set the values as environment
#  variables (MONGODB_URI, JWT_SECRET, ...). The .dockerignore keeps this file out
#  of the image, so `spring.config.import` finds nothing and the env vars win.
#
#  These are plain Spring property keys and OVERRIDE application-prod.yml.
#  ⚠️  An empty value STILL overrides — a blank `app.jwt.secret=` here beats the
#      JWT_SECRET env var and the app won't start. So every line is commented:
#      uncomment ONLY the ones you actually want this file to set.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Atlas connection string, NO trailing /database:
#   mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority
#spring.data.mongodb.uri=

# A long random string. The app REFUSES TO START if this is "test123".
#app.jwt.secret=

# Database name within the cluster (default: prod).
#spring.data.mongodb.database=prod

#app.jwt.expiration-minutes=1440

# The admin account is the one already in the DB (LegacyDataMigration promotes it to
# ADMIN/ACTIVE). New accounts self-register at /api/auth/register and wait for admin
# approval. There is no admin bootstrap config.
